    "findings": [
      "The seven formal pages and connected map/reverse index consistently cover one trait across the three actual Infantry Autogun marks. Their UI names, restriction, and icon association agree with the scoped evidence.",
      "A qualifying sprint dodge from an incoming hit-scan attack queues the player event. The one-second speed proc starts at non-local event processing, repeated qualifying events refresh the same window, and stat/cache updates govern when movement reads it; the text does not promise same-frame speed or a separate 0.2-second stat delay.",
      "The speed formula treats same-type sprint speed contributions additively. The controlled example correctly computes 100*(1+0.20+0.15)=135 versus 120 before the blessing, a 12.5% relative increase. The angle stat combines by maximum, not addition; the 70-degree base source is directly cited, ordinary side-angle comparison is strict, and the separate run-away branch correctly uses signed direction without front/back folding.",
      "Tier I-IV values and RAW strings/formatter reconstruction agree, including the one-second duration and correct delimiter. The RAW omission of the III/IV angle effect is described as an implementation addition rather than a textual contradiction.",
      "The source metadata empty icon fields remain distinct from the validated effective generic UI fallback; the fallback path and attachment URL match the image evidence. The preserved original research trio is unchanged, while the canonical config and extension draft carry the generator-compatible single restriction string."
    ],
